				<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Great news coming from the <strong>Billboard Dance Club Songs Chart</strong>: <strong>Madonna</strong>&#8216;s <strong>Bitch I&#8217;m Madonna </strong>is <strong>Hot Shot Debut</strong> at #<strong>26</strong>! (Music issue: July 4, 2015)<br />
<strong>Ghosttown</strong> down to #<strong>43</strong>.</p>
<p>Keep on requesting <strong>BITCH I&#8217;M MADONNA</strong>!</p>
<p><strong>Bitch I&#8217;m Madonna</strong> is her 5th highest debut after Secret debuted at #18, Nothing Really Matters at #21, Give Me All Your Luvin&#8217; and Causing A Commotion at #24, Hung Up at #25, Like A Virgin and Keep It Together at #26, tied with BIM.<br />
(Thanks to Albert AJ for this info.)</p>
<p>The post <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com/billboard-dance-club-songs-chart-hot-shot-debut-for-bitch-im-madonna/20150619">Billboard Dance Club Songs Chart: Hot Shot Debut for Bitch I&#8217;m Madonna</a> appeared first on <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com">Madonna news new album Rebel Heart</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
